#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / OpenSSL Specification
PACKAGE: openssl
LANGUAGE: C
STATUS: W2
ROLE: Cryptography, TLS, certificate and secure transport foundation

## PROGRAM
OpenSSL provides established cryptographic algorithms, protocols, certificate handling, and secure transport interfaces used throughout the system.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream OpenSSL / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: application -> crypto/TLS API -> provider/configuration -> cryptographic implementation
WHITE_EDITION: safe configuration and integration overlay

## SPEC
- preserve interoperability
- use established primitives
- maintain secure validation defaults
- keep provider/configuration explicit
- track upstream security fixes

## QUALITY
TEST: upstream regression, TLS interoperability, certificate validation, negative paths, provider configuration, upgrade/rollback
ECONOMY: footprint, load behavior, TLS CPU/memory

## SOURCE POLICY
OpenSSL is primarily C. No new cryptographic primitive should be introduced for White Edition. Native patches require a concrete security/correctness/compatibility case and regression evidence.
